    {
      "id": "claim_97cdf3c40aac458d88f7f2f72f997a94",
      "statement": "approval_identity.go states it is the canonical source for the rule that exactly one piece of state, the (candidateKey, sourceEpoch) pair, answers whether an approval has already been answered; before this design (removed in v0.7), the same job was split across three mechanisms with conflicting definitions of 'same question' (a timer-expiring option signature, a permanently-marked full-block hash, and a manual-dismiss question hash), and TestApprovalSuppressionStateIsSingleSource enforces in source that a mis-display fix must not add a second suppression mechanism.",
      "evidence": [
