      "statement": "As of a 2026-08-27 decision, an answered-approval record is carried across user turns for as long as the answered block can still be extracted from the live VT mirror, not bounded by a fixed reply count as it previously was; the accepted tradeoff is that a byte-identical reissued question does not reopen the approval panel while the earlier answered copy is still visible on screen, judged better than the prior fixed-turn-count rule's guaranteed reappearance by the third turn.",
